WEBVTT

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.270
<b>Happy New Year</b>

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.930
<i>It's winter break.</i>

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.570
<i>School and work...</i>

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.110
<i>As I went from one to the other,</i>

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.600
<i>the days passed quickly.</i>

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:28.810
<i>Did the Yokai Apartments really exist?</i>

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.230
<i>Did I really live there for six months?</i>

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:37.690
<i>I thought those memories would 
become a part of me, eventually.</i>

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.650
<i>But now, I can't believe it!</i>

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:44.340
<i>Ryu-san!</i>

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:27.790
<b>Fifth Haunting 
A Place to Call Home</b>

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.410
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.460
Hey, Tashiro,

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:35.150
I listed the props we need for the 
English Club's end-of-year thing.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:36.880
<b>Prop List 

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:36.880
Will this do it?

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:39.810
Seems fine.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:41.550
Take a closer look!

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.790
We're the ones who'll have a hard 
time if anything is missing.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.800
I know that!

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.980
And lately, you've been weird, Inaba.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.400
Like you're forcing yourself 
to work harder...

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.500
I've always been like this.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.470
Check that list carefully.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.620
It's cold! Close the window!

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.130
Sorry, sorry!

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.230
Is something wrong?

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.550
N-Nothing.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.810
<i>Without realizing, I found 
myself looking for them.</i>

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.910
<i>Shadows in the classroom corners.</i>

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.350
<i>Tree branches waving in the wind.</i>

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.600
<i>"Maybe the yokai are out there," I told myself.</i>

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.020
<i>But I couldn't ever find them.</i>

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:41.140
Because over time, nothing ever 
stays exactly the same.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:46.490
<i>But is that really right?</i>

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:51.070
I'm home.

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.320
Welcome back.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:54.990
I'm home.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.940
I'm so hungry!

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.080
Want to get some food, Kaga-san?

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.850
I think they're serving tonkatsu today.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.200
I love that!

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.000
What about you?

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.500
When you eat meat, you feel powerful—

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.110
You're annoying!

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.530
I don't care what you eat.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.760
And you shouldn't care what I like.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.230
Or what?

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.740
Is this some kind of important, 
Earth-shaking news?

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:35.220
N-No... I just wanted to talk—

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.210
I know that!

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.190
You look down on me, don't you?

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:42.380
You think I'm boring and don't 
know how to talk to others!

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.680
No! I don't think that!

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.490
You really want to involve me in 
other people's worlds this way?!

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:52.230
Do you think you're special?

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.820
He got mad...

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.290
What a weirdo.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.370
Leave him alone.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.700
Best to let sleeping dogs lie.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.330
B-But...

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.910
<i>And so, the days passed,</i>

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.630
<i>whether I wanted them to or not.</i>

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.580
<i>Joy... Sadness...</i>

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.070
<i>All of it recedes into the past</i>

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.380
<i>and becomes a memory.</i>

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:51.540
<i>And the more fun the memory, 
the more vague it is.</i>

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.990
<i>And the sooner it slips through your fingers.</i>

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.480
<i>This...</i>

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:04.450
<i>This is the normal life I wanted, right?</i>

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:06.760
I'm heading back now.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:07.840
What's for dinner today?

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.450
No, I'll pass today.

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:13.030
If I don't eat at home today, 
my wife will divorce me!

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:16.100
Anyway, the drinks there are so good...

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.290
I'm in love!

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:20.790
Really, boss?

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.800
Of course. You'll love it.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:24.190
Drink all you want!

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.700
You're the best, boss.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.400
S-Sato-san!

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.740
Yushi-kun...

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.740
How have you been?

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:39.500
How's the new dorm?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.880
Being in a brand-new building must be nice!

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.070
Did you go skiing over winter break?

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.700
Everyone at the apartments is fine.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:51.540
They're always wondering about you.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:54.790
You never contact us at all.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:57.970
I keep saying there's nothing 
to worry about, but...

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.430
It really wasn't a dream.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.010
That apartment building...

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.390
Everyone...

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.570
Why don't we get some food, Yushi-kun?

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.020
I know a great Japanese place.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.160
Okay, here it is!

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.530
The oden here is so good.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:21.130
I could eat a whole plate of the tofu.

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:22.580
Oh, ma'am...

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.330
I'll take the sashimi plate 
and kabayaki unagi.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:28.800
Some mixed vegetables and 
yakitori with sauce.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.040
And a rice bowl, like always.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.430
Thank you very much.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.240
Eat up, Yushi-kun!

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:36.890
Right.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.990
I-It's great!

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:44.670
Isn't it?

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.760
She's almost as good as Ruriko-chan, right?

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.750
But is ditching those people 
from your company okay?

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.550
It's fine!

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:54.660
<b>Sorry. 
Catch you next time!</b>

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.610
They trust me!

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:55.620
<b>You'd better.</b>

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.490
I've worked for Soir Cosmetics 
for twenty years.

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:03.320
And all the girls love me, the #1 
nice middle-management guy!

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:04.990
Section Chief!

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:07.970
They call me "Silver-Haired Sato."

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.410
Nice middle-management guy?

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.350
Ma'am, I'll take another beer.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:15.730
Thank you. Coming right up.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.690
<i>Sato-san's a yokai,</i>

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:22.440
<i>but for years, he's worked 
at a human company.</i>

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:28.840
<i>Actually, he's been living with 
humans for centuries.</i>

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:33.000
<i>He works at a company for years,</i>

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:37.300
<i>leaves, and goes to another one.</i>

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:40.990
<i>He works pretty hard</i>

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:43.040
<i>and has a pretty nice life.</i>

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:47.650
<i>He has a good, steady job, 
and lives a quiet life.</i>

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:51.960
<i>That, he says, is his image 
of the ideal human.</i>

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:55.190
Hey, Sato-san...

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:01.720
Why do you live as a human?

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:09.470
I wanted to be born as a human.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:14.300
Humans have limited lifespans, don't they?

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:18.350
The way they live as hard as they 
can in that time is so beautiful.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:20.650
I've always loved it.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.170
My end's going to come eventually, right?

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:28.940
When that time comes, I want
a girl who will live as a human.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:32.480
Then I'll marry her, we'll have
a child together, and grow old.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:36.330
I think that'd be so nice!

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:40.590
Aren't humans great, Yushi-kun?

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.850
Yushi-kun?

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.450
Humans aren't that great...

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:54.300
I appreciate that you feel that way. 
But we aren't like you think.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.620
Did something happen?

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:00.650
Bad things... A lot of them...

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.310
And I couldn't do anything!

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:09.200
I'm not worthy of hearing you 
say those things about us!

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:15.340
I couldn't save Takenaka... 
And I can't befriend Kaga-san.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:22.330
Then, just change.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.380
Change?

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:27.010
I've changed!

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:29.060
Otherwise, I wouldn't last at the company.

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:33.230
We yokai live a long time, so I know this.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:36.600
Sure, this might be a bad time for anyone,

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:38.490
but better days will come.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:43.570
And it's kids like you who 
form the next generation.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:50.870
Even your bad and ugly 
parts are still human.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:53.860
You can't just cut those parts off.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:55.420
However,

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:58.250
you can change them.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.810
So you need to look to the future.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:03.260
The future...

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.690
That's right. Your dreams.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:09.130
In your finite time, the possibilities are limitless!

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:12.570
And once you start dreaming, 
you need to go forward.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:16.720
And to do that, it's okay 
to get a little greedy.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:20.730
As a human, isn't that your right?

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:25.080
Ryu-san once said the same thing to me.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.510
Huh?!

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:29.020
And I was so sure I sounded cool!

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:32.100
He's human, but he's lived 
a long time, you know...

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:34.700
Jeez!

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:37.850
Um...

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:38.900
Ma'am, I'll take a beer!

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.610
How is Ryu-san, anyway?

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:40.260
Right, coming!

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.010
Tell me!

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.010
Sato-san!

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:58.940
Hey, Mizuki, what's Inaba-kun 
been up to lately?

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.650
He stopped coming over.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:04.020
Who cares?

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.830
Leave him alone.

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:07.210
He's busy with high school.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.870
It feels kind of lonely.

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:16.310
<i>When his parents died, he stopped 
showing any vulnerability.</i>

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:20.830
<i>It's always felt like he was 
holding something in.</i>

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:25.340
<i>Once he decides to do something, 
he never changes his mind.</i>

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:30.450
But would it kill him to ask 
me for help, just once?

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:33.210
As a man, part of being a friend 
is watching over them.

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:34.860
Dad!

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.460
Yushi is at a crossroads now.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:39.530
He's looking for the place he belongs.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:42.430
For now, believe in him and wait.

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:44.870
Yeah.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.380
Nothing. Don't worry about it.

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:51.280
Mizuki was crying and saying he 
wanted you to visit more often!

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:53.070
That's right...

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:55.910
He's so spoiled, unlike you!

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:57.760
Who are you talking to?

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.260
Yushi-kun!

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.250
Put me on, now!

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:07.690
Inaba!

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:15.440
Hey!

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:20.190
Ow.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.330
What?

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:37.470
And so, get this...

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:40.760
At the very end, Tashiro screws up.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.910
Oh, Tashiro's this girl in my club.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:47.400
So the serious scene is ruined, 
and everyone starts laughing.

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.860
I ended up laughing, too!

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:52.470
Jeez, what's that girl's problem, you know?

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:55.770
Looks like you're better than expected.

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:59.820
I talked to someone who's 
lived a lot longer than me,

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.800
and I feel better now, I guess.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:04.900
And since it's been forever, 
I wanted to talk to you, too.

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:13.240
Seeing people face-to-face and 
talking is important, right?

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.710
Yeah.

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:18.450
You won't find any answers 
just sitting by yourself.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:23.790
Because they have different values,
 some people won't debate others.

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:28.460
That means they don't want to hear 
any ideas which aren't theirs, right?

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.470
But that isn't good enough.

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:33.510
Values only have

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:37.810
meaning as values after you compare 
them to someone else's.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:42.070
That's why you have to meet lots of 
people and hear lots of opinions.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.900
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:47.820
<i>so many different people, almost too 
different, were at the Yokai Apartments.</i>

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.620
Hase, you really are smart.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.010
Of course.

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:56.420
Are you still bossing people 
around at school?

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:58.090
Of course!

00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:01.230
Connections are the most 
important thing in life!

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:04.040
I... I see.

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:05.870
Just wait...

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:08.480
Someday, I'll be better than my dad.

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:12.750
No, I need to show my older 
sister who's boss, first.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:19.830
And for that, I need people by my 
side who can get things done.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:23.490
So, a guy I can count on is 
at the next school over.

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:26.060
First, I'll get him on my side.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:28.830
You haven't changed a bit, huh?

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:33.080
Bye.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:35.220
I had fun today.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:36.350
Same here.

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:37.750
Bye.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.150
Write more letters.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:44.790
I'll be waiting.

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:46.500
Okay.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:03.680
See you.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.970
<i>I knew Hase wouldn't change.</i>

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:11.860
<i>He always thinks his own thoughts 
and walks on his own two feet,</i>

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:15.230
<i>heading toward the future of his dreams.</i>

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:22.450
<i>Then, what about me?</i>

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.750
Inaba, are you in?

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:27.980
Yeah.

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:30.330
You've got a visitor.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:36.310
<i>Who wants to see me?</i>

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.110
Eri-chan?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.360
It's been a while.

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:44.880
What's wrong?

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:49.520
You didn't show up once. 
Not for Obon or New Year's.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.060
Are you never coming back?

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:54.140
Coming back?

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:56.770
I went to the Obon service.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.280
Did you put on weight?

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.760
I've been working so much.

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:06.170
I was hoping you'd say I'd put on muscle.

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:18.590
<i>What's wrong?</i>

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:21.470
<i>Did I do something to make her mad?</i>

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:22.810
This...

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:25.520
The postcard you sent.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.130
The first one after you left.

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.780
"I'm doing well.

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:37.230
All the people at the building 
are interesting.

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:41.870
The chef is really good, and I'm happy.

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:44.300
School is fun, too.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.990
I joined the English Conversation Club."

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.950
This is good writing.

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:52.880
I-It is?

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:58.000
When I read this, I thought to 
myself, for the first time...

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:03.560
"I guess even Yushi can have fun sometimes."

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:10.610
I knew that you were always keeping
your feelings bottled up inside.

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:15.460
That you kept us out of your problems.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:22.380
But I said to myself, "So what?

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:25.500
I have my own problems I'm keeping in."

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.120
Yeah.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:30.620
It wasn't that I didn't like you.

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:34.550
I just didn't want to live with you.

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:36.710
Yeah.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:38.990
When you left

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.700
and sounded so happy,

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:46.390
I realized how miserable you 
must've been with us...

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:50.570
And when I thought

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:56.330
that you'd never come home
for summer break or New Year's...

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:01.290
When I thought that, I...

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:08.670
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry, Yushi-kun!

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:10.030
I'm sorry!

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:26.430
<i>It felt like all the filth was being 
cleansed from my heart.</i>

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:29.520
<i>The old barrier between us</i>

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:31.860
<i>disappeared, like it had never been.</i>

00:19:33.890 --> 00:19:40.730
<i>But would my old self have been able 
to accept Eriko's apology like this?</i>

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:59.540
<i>I want to learn more about 
who I am, as a human.</i>

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:04.960
<i>I want to improve myself!</i>

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:09.490
<i>So...</i>

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:12.300
<i>One more time!</i>

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:29.830
Thank you for everything!

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:41.350
<i>A ten-minute walk from 
Takanodai Higashi Station.</i>

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:45.330
<i>A 3-square-meter room with wooden floors
and a 10-square-meter Japanese-style room.</i>

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:46.380
<i>Southern exposure.</i>

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:50.280
<i>The toilet and bath are shared, 
but it comes with food.</i>

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:54.940
<i>The building's name is Kotobuki-so.</i>

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:56.960
<i>Also known as</i>

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:00.800
<i>the Yokai Apartments!</i>

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:04.580
Welcome back.

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:10.170
Hanako-san?

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:25.580
Welcome back!

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.090
I'm home!

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:14.160
Ruriko-san's cooking really is the best!

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:16.760
I'm so glad to be back at 
the Yokai Apartments!

00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:19.810
Master, I'm happy to meet you, as well!

00:23:19.810 --> 00:23:21.040
I see! I see!

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:22.370
Wait, who are you?

00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:26.430
Wait till next episode to find out...

00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:29.720
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:31.140
Petit Hierozoicon.

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:31.720
<b>Sixth Haunting 
Petit Hierozoicon</b>

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:32.460
Petit?

00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:34.270
I bet that's another weird one...

00:23:34.270 --> 00:23:35.860
"Ha," I say!
